         '**Copper anode (active):** neither anion is discharged. The copper atoms of the anode lose electrons more easily, so **the anode dissolves**: ' + ie('Cu(s) -> Cu^2+(aq) + 2e^-') + '. No gas forms; the blue colour stays the same, because every Cu²⁺ removed at the cathode is replaced at the anode.',
